// Windows resource script: embeds app.ico as the executable's icon.
//
// Two entries are needed, not one - they serve different consumers:
//   - Numeric ID 1: Explorer shows the icon group with the LOWEST numeric ID as the
//     .exe file's own icon in the file listing/properties.
//   - The literal name "GLFW_ICON": GLFW's Win32 backend looks up a resource by this
//     exact string name (see glfw's win32_window.c, `LoadImageW(..., L"GLFW_ICON",
//     IMAGE_ICON, ...)`) to use as the window/taskbar icon while running - it does NOT
//     just take the lowest-ID icon the way Explorer does, so a numeric-ID-only entry
//     shows up correctly in Explorer but silently falls back to the default Win32
//     icon in the taskbar/titlebar once the app is actually running.
1 ICON "app.ico"
GLFW_ICON ICON "app.ico"
